comments.body:
@SachaKefif Thanks for confirming the CPU reproduction. Yes, please go ahead with a fix and regression coverage, and reference #193661 in the PR. Device-generic coverage for the shared reduction-fusion path would be ideal if practical. This remains in triage review because it is a silent-correctness issue.

(Follow-up posted by Codex.)

[Human note] Just to be clear, while I’m supportive of this, I’m not volunteering to review these PRs. Codex drafted these comments during triage, and they seemed reasonable at the time. Looking back, though, I realize they could easily be interpreted as me signing up to review them. I’ll avoid leaving comments like this going forward. Sorry for the confusion!

